# Input
```jsx
/* should generate diagnostics */
Promise.all([<div>{await promise}</div>, anotherPromise]);
Promise.all([<Foo bar={await promise} />, anotherPromise]);

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid.jsx:2:20 lint/nursery/noAwaitInPromiseMethods ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  ! This await delays the call to Promise.all().
  
    1 │ /* should generate diagnostics */
  > 2 │ Promise.all([<div>{await promise}</div>, anotherPromise]);
      │                    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    3 │ Promise.all([<Foo bar={await promise} />, anotherPromise]);
    4 │ 
  
  i The rest of the array and the call to Promise.all() have to wait until this promise finishes, so the promises don't run at the same time.
  
  i Move the await into an async function that you call right away, or use .then() instead.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

```

